<% content_for :title, "BMI Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  BMI calculator page (spec issue #53, DESIGN.md BLEND). A two-mode calculator: a
  unit-system segmented control (US / Metric) picks the formula and which height inputs show.
  The form posts over Turbo and re-renders the #result region in place; it works
  WITHOUT JS — the canonical posted fields are inputs[weight], inputs[height] (total
  inches for US, cm for metric) and the checked inputs[unit_system]. With JS, US mode
  offers friendlier feet + inches helper fields (no name → never posted) that the
  bmi_controller sums into the canonical height field, and swaps the weight unit affix.

  Layout per DESIGN.md §3 — an input column + a results panel (≈380px 1fr), collapsing
  to one column on mobile. Spacing scale ("targets not minimums"):
    • unit-system segmented control → halves tight on the Affix tier (gap-1)
    • stacked fields    → space-y-5
    • mode → fields → submit (major blocks) → mt-8 (Section tier)
    • column gutters / card padding → gap-8 / p-7–p-8 (Layout tier)
%>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Fitness &amp; Health</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">BMI Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Body Mass Index from your weight and height, in US or metric units, with the World
    Health Organization adult classification band. Every answer is computed server-side.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/bmi", scope: :inputs, method: :post,
          data: { controller: "bmi", bmi_weight_units_value: { us: "lb", metric: "kg" }.to_json } do |f| %>

      <%# Unit-system selector — a mode/variant picker with N=2 short options, so per the
          picker rule it is a SEGMENTED CONTROL: one connected horizontal track, the two
          options as halves, the active half filled/lifted (NOT the wrapping pill row that
          scrunched the two chips). Reuses the existing segmented-control vocabulary from
          the Percentage page's increase/decrease toggle — a bg-tinted bordered track with
          the two halves tight on the Affix tier (gap-1, parts of one control — DESIGN.md
          §3), each half a `.direction-pill` that lifts to surface white when chosen.
          Native radio <fieldset>/<legend> with peer sr-only radios posting
          inputs[unit_system]; the active half is painted by peer :checked (the no-JS
          baseline) and .is-active (the bmi_controller's paintPills hook), so it works
          without JS and the controller's field show/hide is unchanged. %>
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Unit system</legend>
        <div class="mt-1.5 flex gap-1 rounded-[11px] border border-border-input bg-bg p-1">
          <% [["us", "US units"], ["metric", "Metric units"]].each_with_index do |(value, text), i| %>
            <%= f.radio_button :unit_system, value,
                  checked: i.zero?,
                  class: "peer sr-only",
                  data: { bmi_target: "systemInput", action: "bmi#select" } %>
            <%= f.label :unit_system, text, value: value,
                  class: "direction-pill",
                  data: { bmi_target: "pill", system: value } %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <%# Fields. Weight is shared; height is per-system. Stacked tier: space-y-5. %>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-5">
        <%# Weight — shared across both systems; the unit affix swaps (lb ↔ kg) with the
            mode. The Affix tier (gap-2) sits the unit next to its field (DESIGN.md §3). %>
        <div>
          <%= f.label :weight, "Weight", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_weight" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :weight, id: "inputs_weight", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="w-7 text-sm font-bold text-label" data-bmi-target="weightUnit" aria-hidden="true">lb</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Height (metric) — a single centimetres field. Carries the canonical
            inputs[height] name. Hidden by default in markup so the no-JS baseline shows
            exactly ONE height field (US, the default system) and the two inputs[height]
            fields never both post and clobber each other; the controller toggles which
            system's block shows. (No-JS users compute in the default US units; switching
            systems is the JS enhancement — DESIGN.md §0 progressive enhancement.) %>
        <div data-bmi-target="field" data-bmi-systems="metric" hidden>
          <%= f.label :height, "Height", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_height_cm" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :height, id: "inputs_height_cm", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="w-7 text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">cm</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Height (US). Progressive enhancement with exactly ONE height affordance per
            path (DESIGN.md §0 — server-rendered, progressively enhanced):
              • No JS  → the canonical "Total height in inches" field (visible by default);
                         the ft+in helpers stay hidden (they're inert without the
                         controller, which sums them).
              • With JS → bmi_controller reveals the ft+in helpers and hides the raw
                         total-inches field, summing ft×12 + in into the canonical field. %>
        <div data-bmi-target="field" data-bmi-systems="us">
          <%# Feet + inches helpers — hidden until JS reveals them. NO name → never posted;
              the controller writes their sum into the canonical height field below. Each
              gets a real <label> (DESIGN.md §6 — a label for every input) carrying its
              unit, so the affix is the label and no separate ft/in span is needed. %>
          <div data-bmi-target="feetInches" hidden>
            <span class="field-label">Height</span>
            <div class="mt-1.5 grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-3 gap-y-4">
              <div>
                <%= f.label :feet, "Feet", class: "sr-only", for: "inputs_height_feet" %>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                  <%= f.number_field :feet, name: nil, id: "inputs_height_feet", step: "any",
                        inputmode: "decimal", min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input",
                        data: { bmi_target: "feet", action: "bmi#syncHeight" } %>
                  <span class="w-7 text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">ft</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div>
                <%= f.label :inches, "Inches", class: "sr-only", for: "inputs_height_inches" %>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                  <%= f.number_field :inches, name: nil, id: "inputs_height_inches", step: "any",
                        inputmode: "decimal", min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input",
                        data: { bmi_target: "inches", action: "bmi#syncHeight" } %>
                  <span class="w-7 text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">in</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <%# Canonical total-inches field — the no-JS affordance (visible by default), the
              JS write-target (hidden by the controller). data-bmi-target=usHeight lets the
              controller write the summed ft×12 + in total here. %>
          <div data-bmi-target="totalInches">
            <%= f.label :height, "Total height in inches", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_height_in" %>
            <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
              <%= f.number_field :height, id: "inputs_height_in", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                    min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input",
                    data: { bmi_target: "usHeight" } %>
              <span class="w-7 text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">in</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target) ─────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
